{"title":"1999 JBMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fc2ee1b7f461f0a5e4f97906439c07ad475386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" /> be five real numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/8/678545577d29b03fd9bc41347ab217f465b81b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 + ax + y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d8a5453774d5cf72ef54946bccabcc2a1410d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^3 + bx + y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/e/2aeac52f5e374b6ef155f0c1b5760c94499fd2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c^3 + cx + y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are all distinct numbers prove that their sum is zero.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> we define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937979ea88def8280a252cdabebe496a6f3cfec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n = 2^{3n}+3^{6n+2}+5^{6n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"17\" />. Find the greatest common divisor of the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe35a44df8ba2e1c1f76e0d99d50ee0a688c3e14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0,A_1,\\ldots, A_{1999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a square with the side length 20 and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of points formed with the vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and another 1999 points lying inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that there exists a triangle with vertices in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and with area at most equal with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8dbb0a8f5da75c132c9b538cd88640e7265cfffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 1{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/4/e74396fc64617764366b4b561b23076f0cd95dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D\\in[BC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> be a point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b926e4e40305a2a5122d94b3596791d70c034aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC&gt;BD&gt;DC&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"170\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/9/1c96a161b0d48a88aa46ba002023cc7ead367c73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{C}_1,\\mathcal{C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"16\" /> be the circumcircles of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2ae0e30605dc87c83aecb3f588afa7129bee6aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BB&#39;$\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b7058f8a28ca225136b284b337138a54e39e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CC&#39;$\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be diameters in the two circles, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6aeaf3b3ed66bc4256b58d8123fbf178f31df9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B&#39;C&#39;$\" width=\"37\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acaec668cae1034cab26db5d97863b234480f9b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> is constant (i.e. it does not depend on the choice of the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />).\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO\" title=\"1999 JBMO\">1999 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems\">1998 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2000 JBMO Problems\">2000 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018044444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.078 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 176/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 828/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 68/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4720/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.349      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    7.349      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16663:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018044444 and revision id 97401. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}